# Images: without Width or Height an image has its natural size, 0.75 points per pixel.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: Images · Natural size
	Page:
		Paper: A4
		Margin: 20mm
	Section:
		Text: Images
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Natural size
		Paragraph: The value of `Image` is the path of the file under `images/` of the resources. Without `Width` or `Height`, a PNG or a JPEG measures 0.75 points per pixel and an SVG what its `width` and `height` say. An image does not shrink on its own: one wider than its container is an error.
